---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import GuideLayout from '../../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';

import shotCounsellor from '../../../assets/guide/11-student-counsellor.png';
---

<GuideLayout
  slug="student-booking"
  title="Book a session with your counsellor"
  description="Finding a time, what happens after you book, and how to reach your counsellor between sessions."
  audience="For students"
  readingTime="2 min read"
>
  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">1</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Open My Counsellor</h2>
      <p>
        Tap <strong>My Counsellor</strong> from your dashboard. This page shows who you have been
        assigned, what they specialise in, which languages they speak, and whether they see students
        by video, in person, or both.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <strong>Assigned</strong> badge next to their name means your school has matched you
        already. There is nothing to choose.
      </p>
      <figure>
        <Image
          src={shotCounsellor}
          alt="The My Counsellor page showing an assigned counsellor with their title, years of experience, specialisms, languages and a Book Session button."
          loading="eager"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Your class is shown here too, because that is what your counsellor is assigned to.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">2</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Press Book Session</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Book Session</strong> opens your counsellor's calendar in a new tab, showing the
        times they have free. Pick one that works and confirm.
      </p>
      <div class="guide-note guide-privacy">
        <p>
          <strong>Your name and email go to the booking calendar</strong> so your counsellor knows
          who is coming and can send you the joining link. That is the only thing shared at this
          step, and it is filled in for you so you do not have to type it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">3</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>What happens next</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The session appears under <strong>Upcoming Sessions</strong> on this page.</li>
        <li>Your dashboard shows it at the top as your next session.</li>
        <li>
          If it is a video session, the joining link comes through on the booking confirmation.
        </li>
        <li>
          Need to change it? Use the reschedule or cancel link on the same confirmation rather than
          booking a second slot.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">4</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Message instead, if that is easier</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Send Message</strong> opens a private thread with your counsellor. Some things are
        easier to type than to say out loud, and starting there is completely normal.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you message outside your counsellor's working hours you will get an automatic reply
        telling you when they are back, along with helpline numbers you can call straight away. Your
        message is still waiting for them when they return.
      </p>
      <div class="guide-note">
        <p>
          <strong>Messages are not watched in real time.</strong> Your counsellor reads them during
          their working hours. If something cannot wait, call Tele-MANAS on <strong>14416</strong>
          or emergency services on <strong>112</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-footer">
    <h2>Things worth knowing</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>You do not have to prepare anything.</strong> Turning up with "I do not really know
      where to start" is a completely normal way to begin a first session.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Your teachers are not told that you booked.</strong> See
      <a href="/resources/guide/student-privacy">what your school can and cannot see</a> for the
      detail of who reads what.
    </p>
    <p>
      If no counsellor is showing on this page yet, your school has not finished setting up your
      class. Ask your class teacher.
    </p>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
